# Cursor rules

- One topic per file: `.cursor/rules/<kebab-case>.mdc` with frontmatter `description`, `globs`, `alwaysApply`.
- Prefer glob-scoped rules with `alwaysApply: false`. Keep always-on rules short; repo-wide conventions belong in `AGENTS.md`.
- Do not repeat `AGENTS.md` or another rule; link to it.
- Learned facts that are not a coding rule go in `docs/agents/learned.md`; personal preferences stay out of the repo.
- Update the index in `.cursor/rules/README.md` when adding, renaming or deleting a rule.
